B.eA8=new A.ej("battery","Battery","\ud83d\udd0b",B.be,"Pushes electric charge round a loop. Tap it to change how many volts it has. More volts means a stronger push.","Two different metals sit in a chemical paste. The chemicals swap electrons between the metals, and that makes a voltage.")
B.eAe=new A.ej("solar","Solar panel","\u2600\ufe0f",B.bt,"Makes electricity from light, with no battery. Use the light slider: more sunshine means more volts.","Slices of silicon. When light hits them it knocks electrons loose, and a layer on each side pushes them one way.")
B.eAT=new A.ej("crank","Hand crank","\ud83d\udd04",B.cP,"A generator you turn by hand. Tap it again and again: the faster you spin it, the more volts it makes.","A magnet spins inside a coil of copper wire. A moving magnet pushes electrons along the wire. This is how an alternator or dynamo works.")
B.eAv=new A.ej("turbine","Wind turbine","\ud83c\udf2c\ufe0f",B.aH,"A generator turned by the wind. Change the wind strength to change the volts.","Blades catch the wind and turn a shaft joined to a generator, the same coil-and-magnet idea as a dynamo.")
B.eA0=new A.ej("buck","Step-down converter","\ud83d\udd3d",B.fK,"Brings the volts DOWN to the number you choose (3, 5, 6 or 9 V), so a gadget that needs few volts is safe on a big battery. The + (left) dot is the input from the battery. The right dot is the output to the gadget. More volts must go in than come out.","A fast switch chops the power into tiny pulses, and a coil and capacitor smooth them out to a lower voltage. Very little energy is wasted as heat.")
B.eAt=new A.ej("regulator","5 V regulator","\ud83e\uddca",B.bP,"Always gives out 5 volts, whatever bigger battery you use. The + (left) dot is the input. It turns the extra volts into HEAT, so it gets hot if the gadget takes a lot of current. Great for a phone, too hot for a big load.","A transistor acts like a tap that closes more when too many volts arrive, and a tiny circuit checks the output many times a second.")
B.eAY=new A.ej("diode","Diode","\u27a1\ufe0f",B.aQ,"Lets electricity go one way only (left to right). It uses up about 0.7 volts. Put it in a loop so a battery connected backwards cannot hurt a gadget.","A join between two kinds of crystal that electrons can cross in one direction but not the other.")
B.eAF=new A.ej("ldr","Light sensor","\ud83c\udf1e",B.ex,"A resistor that changes with light: in the dark it holds the current back, in bright light it lets more through. Tap it and move the Light slider.","A flat disc of a special material (cadmium sulfide) that frees more electrons when light hits it.")
B.eAj=new A.ej("switch","Switch","\ud83c\udf9a\ufe0f",B.bh,"Opens or closes the loop. Electricity only flows round a closed loop. Tap it to flip it.","Two metal contacts. Flipping the lever makes them touch, or pulls them apart.")
B.eAV=new A.ej("fuse","Fuse","\ud83e\uddef",B.bZ,"A safety part. If too much current flows, its thin wire melts and the loop breaks, which stops fires.","A very thin strip of metal inside a glass tube. It heats up and melts when the current is too high.")
B.ezT=new A.ej("pot","Dimmer knob","\ud83c\udf9b\ufe0f",B.fK,"A resistor you can change. Turn it to let less or more current through, like a volume control.","A strip of resistive material with a sliding contact that touches it at different places.")
B.eAG=new A.ej("resistor","Resistor","\u3030\ufe0f",B.aQ,"Holds back the current, which protects other parts. Tap it to change its size in ohms.","A tiny rod of carbon or a thin metal film, with coloured stripes that tell you its ohms.")
B.eAI=new A.ej("bulb","Light bulb","\ud83d\udca1",B.ex,"Glows when current heats its thin wire. It is made for 3 volts. Much more and it burns out!","A very thin coil of tungsten wire in a glass bulb with no air, so it can glow white hot without burning.")
B.eAg=new A.ej("led","LED","\ud83d\udd34",B.aA,"A light that uses very little power. It only works one way round, and it burns out without a resistor to protect it.","A tiny chip of special crystal. When electrons cross the join in the chip they give off light.")
B.eAk=new A.ej("motor","Motor","\u2699\ufe0f",B.bP,"Turns electricity into spinning. More current spins it faster. It is the reverse of a generator.","Coils of wire become magnets when current flows, and they push and pull against fixed magnets to make a shaft turn.")
B.eAC=new A.ej("buzzer","Buzzer","\ud83d\udd14",B.c4,"Makes a sound when current flows through it.","A thin metal disc is pulled and released many times a second by electric pulses. That shakes the air as sound.")
B.eA9=new A.ej("heater","Heater","\ud83d\udd25",B.cP,"Turns electricity into heat. Toasters and kettles work like this. More power makes it glow hotter.","A long coil of special wire that resists the current. The current has to push through it, and that makes it hot.")
B.eAx=new A.ej("capacitor","Capacitor","\ud83e\udeab",B.cs,"Stores electric charge like a tiny rechargeable tank. It fills up from a battery, then can give the charge back.","Two sheets of metal foil, rolled up with a thin plastic sheet between them.")
B.eAp=new A.ej("radio","Radio","\ud83d\udcfb",B.oq,"Needs about 3 volts or more. When it has power it picks up stations and plays them.","An aerial catches invisible radio waves. A tuner picks one station, and a chip turns it back into sound for the speaker.")
B.eAm=new A.ej("tv","Samsung Neo QLED 8K","\ud83d\udcfa",B.ba,"Needs 5.5 to 13.5 volts and the + (left) dot towards the battery +. When it switches on it shows NGMY animation channels. Tap it 3 times quickly to open the big screen.","Millions of tiny red, green and blue lights, called pixels, that glow at different strengths to make every colour.")
B.eA_=new A.ej("voltmeter","Voltmeter","\ud83e\udded",B.bv,"Measures volts. Wire it across a part (one dot each side) to read how many volts that part gets. It never goes in the loop itself.","A very sensitive coil on a needle, behind a huge resistor so almost no current is stolen from the circuit.")
B.eA6=new A.ej("ammeter","Ammeter","\ud83d\udcdf",B.aQ,"Measures how much current is flowing. It goes IN the loop, one after another with the part you are measuring. Never wire it straight across a battery!","A coil on a needle with a tiny resistor, so the current passes through it almost freely.")
B.eAc=new A.ej("fan","Fan","\ud83c\udf00",B.aH,"Spins its blades when it gets 2 to 9 volts. More volts, faster spin. Works either way round.","A small motor turns plastic blades that push the air.")
B.eB_=new A.ej("speaker","Speaker","\ud83d\udd0a",B.c4,"Plays a sound when powered (1.5 to 9 volts). The + dot goes to the battery +.","A coil and magnet shake a paper cone back and forth. The cone pushes the air to make sound.")
B.eAP=new A.ej("clock","Digital clock","\u23f0",B.be,"Shows the real time once it has 2.5 to 7 volts. Too many volts and it burns out. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A quartz crystal ticks exactly 32,768 times a second, and a chip counts the ticks to show the time.")
B.eAs=new A.ej("calculator","Calculator","\ud83e\uddee",B.MP,"Sips power: it works from 1.2 to 4.8 volts. A 9 volt battery would burn it out. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A tiny chip does the sums and a liquid-crystal screen shows the numbers. A little solar cell can power it.")
B.eA5=new A.ej("phone","iPhone 18 Pro Max","\ud83d\udcf1",B.cs,"The newest iPhone with a Dynamic Island. Tap it 3 times for the big phone, 4 times to make it bigger. It charges when it gets 4 to 7 volts (a USB charger gives 5). Too little and it will not charge; too much and it burns. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A lithium battery is filled slowly by a charging chip that keeps the voltage just right.")
B.eAZ=new A.ej("router","WiFi router","\ud83d\udcf6",B.fK,"Needs 8 to 14 volts. Its lights blink when it is working. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A small computer plus a radio that sends and receives the internet through the air.")
B.eB1=new A.ej("siren","Siren","\ud83d\udea8",B.aA,"A loud alarm that needs 5 to 13.5 volts. Lights flash and the sound goes up and down. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A motor spins a mirror that sweeps the light, and an oscillator makes the rising and falling tone.")
B.ezW=new A.ej("toycar","Toy car","\ud83d\ude97",B.cP,"A little motor drives the wheels once it gets 2 to 9 volts. Works either way round.","A small motor turns a gear that spins the back wheels.")
B.eB2=new A.ej("kettle","Kettle","\ud83e\uded6",B.mV,"Boils water with a heating coil. It needs 3 to 13 volts and a strong battery. Watch the steam!","A coil of resistance wire at the bottom heats the water. A thermostat switches it off when it boils.")
B.eA3=new A.ej("lamp","Desk lamp","\ud83e\ude94",B.ex,"A bright lamp that needs 2.5 to 8 volts. It gets brighter with more volts. Works either way round.","A bulb in a bendy arm, with a shade that points the light down at your desk.")
B.eAf=new A.ej("lights","Party lights","\ud83c\udf84",B.oq,"A string of coloured lights that twinkle. They need 3.5 to 13.5 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","Many small bulbs joined along one wire, each with its own colour of glass.")
B.eAq=new A.ej("fridge","Fridge","\ud83e\uddca",B.ha,"Keeps food cold. Needs 4 to 13 volts. When it works the light inside comes on and frost appears. Works either way round.","A pump squeezes a special gas so it gets hot outside the fridge and very cold inside, carrying the warmth away.")
B.ezY=new A.ej("washer","Washing machine","\ud83e\udee7",B.cs,"The drum spins and soap bubbles fly. Needs 5 to 13.5 volts. Works either way round.","A strong motor spins a drum full of water and clothes, back and forth, to shake the dirt out.")
B.eAQ=new A.ej("blender","Blender","\ud83e\udd64",B.bZ,"Sharp blades whizz round and mash the fruit. Needs 2.4 to 10 volts. More volts, faster blades.","A fast motor spins steel blades at the bottom of a jug.")
B.eAn=new A.ej("drone","Drone","\ud83d\ude81",B.bP,"Four rotors lift it off the ground once it gets 5 to 12.5 volts. Works either way round.","Four small motors spin propellers that push air down, so the drone is pushed up.")
B.eA2=new A.ej("drill","Power drill","\ud83d\udd29",B.aQ,"The bit spins and sparks fly. Needs 3.5 to 12 volts. Works either way round.","A strong motor and gears turn the drill bit slowly but with great force.")
B.eAr=new A.ej("torch","Torch","\ud83d\udd26",B.bL,"A torch beam. It needs only 2 to 6 volts. Too many volts and the little bulb pops. Works either way round.","A small bulb sits in a curved mirror that throws the light forward in a beam.")
B.eAN=new A.ej("neon","Neon sign","\ud83e\udea7",B.c4,"A glowing OPEN sign that flickers on. Needs 6 to 13.5 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A glass tube full of neon gas glows when electricity passes through it.")
B.ezZ=new A.ej("microwave","Microwave","\ud83c\udf72",B.cP,"The plate turns and the timer counts down. Needs a lot of power: 8 to 13.5 volts. Works either way round.","A tube makes invisible microwaves that shake the water in food so it gets hot.")
B.eAH=new A.ej("doorbell","Doorbell","\ud83d\udd14",B.bt,"Swings its bell and goes ding-dong. Needs 3 to 12 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A little hammer, pulled by a magnet, hits a metal bar again and again.")
B.eAb=new A.ej("camera","Security camera","\ud83d\udcf7",B.an,"A red REC light blinks and the lens looks around. Needs 4 to 12 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A small sensor turns light into numbers, many times a second, and a chip makes them into a video.")
B.eAB=new A.ej("console","Game console","\ud83c\udfae",B.bh,"Plays a little ball game on its screen. Needs 4.5 to 9.5 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A fast chip draws the picture over and over, many times each second.")
B.eAS=new A.ej("heartmon","Heart monitor","\ud83e\ude7a",B.hv,"Draws a heartbeat line and beeps. Needs 3 to 9 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","Sensors on the body feel tiny electric signals made by the heart and a chip draws them as a line.")
B.ezX=new A.ej("aquarium","Aquarium","\ud83d\udc20",B.ba,"A pump blows bubbles and a fish swims around. Needs 3 to 9 volts. Works either way round.","A small motor pushes air through a stone, making lots of tiny bubbles.")
B.eAw=new A.ej("lighthouse","Lighthouse","\ud83d\uddfc",B.ex,"A bright beam sweeps round and round. Needs 4 to 13.5 volts. Works either way round.","A huge lamp sits inside a glass lens that squeezes the light into a beam. A motor turns the lens.")
B.eAE=new A.ej("discoball","Disco ball","\ud83e\udea9",B.oq,"Spins and throws sparkles everywhere. Needs 5 to 13.5 volts. Works either way round.","Hundreds of tiny mirrors on a ball bounce a spotlight all around the room as it turns.")
B.eAX=new A.ej("robot","Robot","\ud83e\udd16",B.aH,"Its eyes light up and blink, and its arm waves. Needs 4 to 9 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A tiny computer reads sensors and tells small motors in the arms and head what to do.")
B.ezV=new A.ej("toaster","Toaster","\ud83c\udf5e",B.e3,"Glowing wires toast the bread, then it pops up. Needs 3.5 to 13 volts and a strong battery. Works either way round.","Thin wires get red hot as the current squeezes through them and toast the bread.")
B.eB0=new A.ej("ledstrip","LED strip","\ud83c\udf08",B.c4,"A strip of colour-changing lights. Needs 3 to 13.5 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","Many tiny LEDs in red, green and blue sit along a bendy strip. Mixing the three makes every colour.")
B.eAM=new A.ej("pump","Water pump","\ud83d\udeb0",B.aH,"Pushes water round a pipe. Needs 2.5 to 9 volts. Works either way round.","A small motor spins a paddle wheel inside a sealed case and flings water out of the pipe.")
B.eAy=new A.ej("hairdryer","Hair dryer","\ud83d\udca8",B.hM,"Blows warm air. A hungry gadget: it needs 6 to 13 volts and a strong battery. Works either way round.","A fan blows air past a hot coil of wire, the same coil idea as a toaster.")
B.eAK=new A.ej("headphones","Headphones","\ud83c\udfa7",B.bh,"Play music into your ears. They are quiet and need only 1.2 to 5 volts, so 9 volts would burn them. Use a step-down converter! The + dot goes to the battery +.","Two tiny speakers, one for each ear, shake the air with a coil and a thin cone.")
B.eA4=new A.ej("smartwatch","Apple Watch Ultra","\u231a",B.bv,"Shows the time and your heartbeat. It sips power: 3 to 4.5 volts only. Use a step-down converter on bigger batteries. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A tiny chip, a screen and a sensor that shines green light on your wrist to feel your pulse.")
B.eAW=new A.ej("tablet","iPad Pro M5","\ud83d\udcf2",B.cs,"A big screen playing NGMY ads. Needs 4.5 to 7.5 volts, so a 9 volt battery needs a step-down converter. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A bright flat screen, a fast chip and a lithium battery in a thin case.")
B.ezS=new A.ej("lgtv","LG OLED evo G5","\ud83d\udcfa",B.hv,"A premium OLED TV where every pixel makes its own light, so black is truly black. Needs 5.5 to 13.5 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +. Tap it 3 times for the big screen, 4 times to make it bigger.","Each tiny pixel is an organic LED that glows by itself, so there is no backlight at all.")
B.eAo=new A.ej("sonytv","Sony Bravia 9","\ud83d\udcfa",B.bu,"A top Mini LED TV with thousands of tiny lights behind the screen for bright, rich pictures. Needs 5.5 to 13.5 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","Thousands of small LED zones switch on and off to light only the bright parts of the picture.")
B.eAh=new A.ej("appletv","Apple TV 4K","\ud83d\udcfa",B.bO,"A slim silver TV with the Apple TV app screen. Needs 5.5 to 13.5 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A fast chip decodes the video and a very thin panel shows it with wide, rich colour.")
B.eAD=new A.ej("bangtv","Bang and Olufsen Beovision","\ud83d\udcfa",B.wn,"A luxury TV in brushed aluminium with a fabric speaker below the screen. Needs 6 to 13.5 volts. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A hand-finished frame, a big OLED panel and a speaker wrapped in wool fabric.")
B.ezU=new A.ej("iphonefold","iPhone Fold","\ud83d\udcf1",B.b8,"A phone that opens like a book into a big screen. Needs 4 to 7 volts, so a 9 volt battery would burn it: use a step-down converter. The + dot goes to the battery +. Tap 3 times for the big phone, 4 times to make it bigger.","A bendable glass screen folds along a hinge made of tiny gears.")
B.eA7=new A.ej("galaxy","Samsung Galaxy S26 Ultra","\ud83d\udcf1",B.d9,"A top Android phone with a huge flat screen and a punch-hole camera. Needs 4 to 7 volts: use a step-down converter on bigger batteries. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A bright AMOLED screen where each pixel makes its own light, with a titanium frame.")
B.eAU=new A.ej("zfold","Samsung Galaxy Z Fold7","\ud83d\udcf1",B.cF,"A foldable Samsung that opens into a small tablet. Needs 4 to 7 volts: use a step-down converter. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A flexible screen and a strong hinge let it fold flat and open again many thousands of times.")
B.eAz=new A.ej("pixel","Google Pixel 10 Pro XL","\ud83d\udcf1",B.bi,"Google's top phone with a smart camera bar. Needs 4 to 7 volts: use a step-down converter. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A chip made for AI helps the camera and the phone understand what you need.")
B.eAu=new A.ej("xiaomi","Xiaomi 16 Ultra","\ud83d\udcf1",B.c9,"A top Chinese phone built around a big camera. Needs 4 to 7 volts: use a step-down converter. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A one-inch camera sensor catches a lot of light, so photos look good even at night.")
B.eAL=new A.ej("huawei","Huawei Mate 80 Pro Max","\ud83d\udcf1",B.aA,"A premium Huawei flagship with a round camera ring. Needs 4 to 7 volts: use a step-down converter. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A tough glass front, a big battery and a camera made with a famous camera maker.")
B.eAi=new A.ej("oppo","OPPO Find X9 Ultra","\ud83d\udcf1",B.be,"A top OPPO with a super fast charger and two zoom cameras. Needs 4 to 7 volts: use a step-down converter. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A curved glass screen, a big battery and a charger that fills it very quickly.")
B.eAA=new A.ej("honor","Honor Magic V5","\ud83d\udcf1",B.cs,"One of the thinnest foldable phones. Needs 4 to 7 volts: use a step-down converter. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A very thin hinge and a carbon-fibre frame keep it light even when it opens into a big screen.")
B.eAJ=new A.ej("vivo","vivo X300 Pro","\ud83d\udcf1",B.cP,"A premium vivo phone with a pro camera. Needs 4 to 7 volts: use a step-down converter. The + dot goes to the battery +.","A big camera sensor and a special lens system make sharp photos and portraits.")
