B.eRg=new A.y("Movement","The chest muscles push your arms forward, like when you push a door.")
B.eMa=new A.y("Movement","The biceps bends your elbow. When a muscle works it gets shorter and fatter.")
B.ePX=new A.y("Movement","The triceps straightens your elbow. It works opposite the biceps: muscles can only pull, so they come in pairs.")
B.eWi=new A.y("Movement","Long muscles in your forearm pull on tendons that work your fingers, like puppet strings.")
B.f1Y=new A.y("Movement","Your tummy muscles hold your body upright and help you bend and twist.")
B.f63=new A.y("Movement","The muscles at the sides of your waist that help you twist and lean.")
B.eZF=new A.y("Movement","The widest muscle in your back. It pulls your arms down, like when you swim or climb.")
B.eHl=new A.y("Movement","Your bottom muscles are the biggest in your body. They push you up stairs and keep you standing.")
B.eWu=new A.y("Movement","Four muscles at the front of your thigh. Together they are the strongest in your body for lifting weight.")
B.eIf=new A.y("Movement","The muscles at the back of your thigh that bend your knee when you run.")
B.f2d=new A.y("Movement","The calf muscle pushes you up on your toes when you walk, run and jump.")
B.f3k=new A.y("Movement","These lift your foot up so your toes do not drag on the ground.")
B.eWW=new A.y("Nerves","Weighs about 1.4 kg and uses a fifth of your energy. It has around 86 billion nerve cells and runs everything you do.")
B.f2s=new A.y("Hormones","A butterfly-shaped gland in your neck. It makes hormones that control how fast your body uses energy.")
B.eJv=new A.y("Breathing","The trachea carries air down to your lungs. Rings of tough cartilage keep it open.")
B.f3Y=new A.y("Digestion","The oesophagus squeezes food down to your stomach in waves, so you can swallow even upside down.")
B.eNz=new A.y("Breathing","You breathe about 20,000 times a day. Spread flat, your lungs would cover a tennis court.")
B.f1B=new A.y("Blood","About the size of your fist. It beats around 100,000 times a day and pumps blood round a track 100,000 km long.")
B.eQV=new A.y("Breathing","A dome-shaped muscle under your lungs. It pulls down to suck air in. A hiccup is it twitching.")
B.eUH=new A.y("Digestion","Cleans your blood and stores energy. It is the only organ that can grow back after damage.")
B.f__=new A.y("Digestion","A small green pouch that stores bile, a juice that helps you digest fatty food.")
B.f47=new A.y("Digestion","Acid in your stomach could dissolve metal, but a thick layer of mucus protects it.")
B.f4_=new A.y("Blood","Filters old blood cells and helps fight germs. You can live without it.")
B.f43=new A.y("Digestion","Makes juices to digest food and insulin, a hormone that controls the sugar in your blood.")
B.eVf=new A.y("Cleaning","Clean about 180 litres of blood every day and turn the waste into urine.")
B.f_U=new A.y("Digestion","About 6 metres long, folded up in your tummy. This is where most food is turned into energy for your blood.")
B.f14=new A.y("Digestion","Takes the water from what is left and makes the rest into waste. It is about 1.5 metres long.")
B.f3K=new A.y("Cleaning","A stretchy bag that holds urine. It can hold about half a litre.")
B.eWV=new A.y("Nerves","A thick rope of nerves inside your backbone. It carries messages between your brain and the rest of your body.")
